WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:06.120
When it comes to horror movies, you need a
great ending to truly make it epic.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.910
A bad ending can ruin even the scariest of
spooky films, but a great horror movie ending

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.900
can stick with you long after you've left
the theaters.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.140
Here are some truly epic horror movie endings.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.380
Spoilers ahead.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:19.720
Kill List

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:25.340
This story follows two hit men, Jay and Gal,
who are hired to murder three seemingly random

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:25.860
people.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.179
Ultimately, their "kill list" leads them into
the English countryside where they're attacked

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.360
by a creepy cult.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.340
Gal is murdered, and Jay is forced to battle
against a hooded, hunchbacked man.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.760
Jay dispatches his opponent with relative
ease with several stabs to its back, but he's

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.640
shocked when the cloak is pulled back to reveal
his wife.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.300
Worse still, the "hunchback's" bump is actually
their young son, strapped to his mom's back

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.040
as part of an occult ritual.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:06.550
Absolutely stunned that he's just butchered
his family, Jay disappears into his own mind

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:11.100
as the cultists applaud the fight and place
a crown atop his head.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:12.360
The Guest

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:17.430
The chaos begins when army veteran David visits
the family of a fallen comrade.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:22.460
At first, David seems like a cool guy, but
under that charming, hunky exterior, there's

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:25.580
an ultra-aggressive super soldier waiting
to explode.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.620
Several plot turns later, David is chasing
our sibling heroes, Anna and Luke, through

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.480
a high school haunted house, seemingly intent
on doing away with them.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.340
Luckily, Luke gets the upper hand when he
stabs David in the chest.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:42.930
The authorities soon arrive on the scene,
and it looks like Anna and Luke are finally

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:46.740
safe…until a familiar-looking fireman walks
out of the gym.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.460
The Invitation

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:53.900
The story of this creepy film focuses on a
man named Will, who receives a dinner invitation

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.860
from his ex-wife Eden for a dinner party with
some old friends that he hasn't seen in years.

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:03.260
But beneath the polite conversation, Will
can sense there's something strange going

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:07.840
on, all while Eden and her new husband David
are promoting some bizarre cult.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.780
As the evening wears on, Will notices David
walking into the backyard and lighting a red

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.540
lantern.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.640
Soon after, Eden and David start butchering
every guest they can get their hands on.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:24.080
Fortunately, Will survives the assault, but
as he steps outside, he sees something almost

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:24.960
as horrifying.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:39.140
Nearly every house he can see is showing the
same red lantern that David lit earlier, implying

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:43.380
that his dinner party wasn't the only one
to have such a violent dessert.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Krampus

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.340
Fed up and frustrated with his unruly relatives,
a young boy named Max loses the Christmas

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:54.700
spirit, tears up his letter to Santa, and
tosses the shreds out the window.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:03:00.060
Little does Max know he's just summoned a
horned beast named Krampus who plans on punishing

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.160
Max's entire family.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:12.580
But after a heart to heart with the Christmas
demon, Max wakes up to find the whole invasion

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:17.800
was just a dream, and soon, he's peacefully
celebrating Christmas with his entire family.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:24.420
However, Max finds a bell with the word "Krampus"
etched onto the side as his family also seems

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:30.340
to remember the horrible events of what Max
had thought was just some Christmas Eve nightmares.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:35.580
In fact...it doesn't seem like the family
really escaped Krampus' wrath at all.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.200
The Witch

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:42.360
In The Witch, William and his Puritan family
are banished to the wilderness because of

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:47.029
their super-extreme beliefs, and forced to
contend with the supernatural monster that

00:03:47.029 --> 00:03:49.280
seems to be skulking around their new home.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.340
"Peek...boo!"

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:02.680
The witch does a pretty good job of tearing
the family apart, and eventually, the only

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.380
member who isn't dead or missing is eldest
daughter Thomasin.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:11.319
Left all alone in the middle of nowhere and
feeling cut off from the Almighty, Thomasin

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:12.680
strikes a deal with Satan.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:18.020
"Wouldst thou like to live deliciously?"

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:20.760
"Yes."

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:26.720
Following Satan's orders, Thomasin strips
nude and wanders into the woods, where a coven

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.180
of witches rise into the air as Thomasin joins
them.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.400
Shaun of the Dead

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:41.740
This horror-comedy isn't just full of laughs.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:46.560
It also has some genuinely terrifying moments
and a few scenes that will leave you a bit

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:47.900
emotionally raw, too.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:52.880
Honestly, Shaun of the Dead's climax seems
like one of the darkest moments Edgar Wright

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:57.980
has ever directed, as Shaun says goodbye to
his best friend Ed, who's been bitten by a

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:58.480
zombie.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:04:59.720
"What are you talking about?"

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.840
"I’ll only hold you back."

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:03.220
"Yeah, but-"

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:13.140
But in the last scene of the film, Wright
sends the audience off with a bit of the ol'

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:13.720
switcheroo.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:19.150
As it turns out, Shaun's life after the zombie
apocalypse really isn't all that different

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:22.120
from how it was before the zombie apocalypse.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:23.720
“Ed!”

